  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Strengthening tripartite efforts to support the Decent Work Agenda in the Caribbean</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The ILO is currently supporting the development and implementation of Decent Work Country Programmes (DWCPs) in five Caribbean countries (Bahamas, Suriname, Belize, Guyana and Barbados), with two additional DWCPs underway&#x2014;Jamaica, which is in the drafting phase, and Grenada, which is in the validation and approval phase. This process requires strong tripartite dialogue mechanisms to agree on national priorities and to support effective monitoring and implementation.</narrative>
  </description>
